blockd/tests/golden_root_cost.rs, release, macOS arm64 (18 logical cpus, APFS),
median of 3, local file object store. Second platform; the primary run is
raw/golden-root-cost.log (aarch64 Linux container, same platform as the
delta-pack numbers). Same process, same store, same volume
geometry -- the only variable is how a volume gets its rootfs.

  copy      = stream the image into the volume and commit it (what a create did)
  reference = publish the image once, provision by referencing its chunks (ADR-0017)

One create:

 image MiB       path uploaded MiB    objects provision ms    speedup        gen
        64       copy        64.00         19        483.3       1.0x          1
        64  reference         0.00          3         29.4      16.5x          1
        64  (publish)         once          -        502.9          -          -
       256       copy       256.01         67       1836.9       1.0x          1
       256  reference         0.01          3         28.2      65.1x          1
       256  (publish)         once          -       2013.5          -          -
       512       copy       512.01        131       3612.5       1.0x          1
       512  reference         0.02          3         29.0     124.6x          1
       512  (publish)         once          -       2988.5          -          -

N Cats from one image at once (256 MiB image):

    cats       path uploaded MiB    objects        wall ms    speedup
       1       copy       256.01         67         1777.4       1.0x
       1  reference         0.01          3           28.3      62.7x
       4       copy      1024.02        268         6067.7       1.0x
       4  reference         0.04         12          123.2      49.2x
      10       copy      2560.05        670         9614.5       1.0x
      10  reference         0.11         30          250.8      38.3x

Cold read of every chunk on a host with an empty cache (64 MiB):

        path       cold read ms              MiB/s
        copy              130.3                491
   reference              131.0                489

Reading:

* Provisioning cost is now independent of image size (~29 ms), because it writes
  map nodes and a commit record and nothing else. The 0.01-0.02 MiB "uploaded"
  is those map nodes.
* Concurrent creates no longer contend on the object store at all: 10 Cats upload
  0.11 MiB between them instead of 2.5 GiB.
* Referencing a shared chunk costs nothing to read: a provisioned chunk is one
  object, exactly like a private one, so cold-read throughput is unchanged
  (491 vs 489 MiB/s, within noise).
* The `copy` column here is the engine-level copy, not the old path that streamed
  the image through an NBD socket, so these speedups are conservative.
* Publishing an image costs ~3 s for 512 MiB and happens once per image digest.
  Today it happens on the first launch that uses the image, so that launch pays
  it; pre-publishing at image-deploy time would remove even that.

Also found by this bench: `ChunkEngine::detach` joined a lease-renewal thread that
was sleeping out lease_ttl_ms/3, so every detach -- every stop, suspend and cold
migration, per volume -- waited ~1.67 s at the default TTL. Before the fix every
row above had a 1674 ms floor, which is what made it visible. Renewal now waits on
a condvar; regression test: engine::tests::detaching_does_not_wait_out_the_lease_renewal_interval.
